---
title: Apple Pie
description: As British as...
servings: 6
prep time: 20m
cook time: 35m
course: Dessert
locale: en_GB
difficulty: Medium
cuisine: British
diet: Vegetarian
tags:
- british
- sweet
- dessert
- vegetarian
- pie
---

Preheat the oven to 200°C.

Lightly stew the @bramley apples{5}(peeled, cored and quartered) in the microwave on high for ~{5%minutes}. Allow to cool.

Sieve the @plain flour{400%g} and @salt{pinch} into a bowl. Rub in the @butter{220%g} until the mixture resembles fine breadcrumbs.

Mix the @cold water{50%ml} into the flour mixture using a knife, and then by hand firm up the mixture. The pastry should be of an even colour and suitable consistency for rolling.

Lightly dust the work surface and rolling pin with flour. Divide the pastry into two halves. Take one half and roll it out so that it is big enough to cover a #25 cm enamel or aluminium plate{}. Trim the edges with a knife, using the edges of the plate as a guide.

Cover the pastry with the stewed apples and sprinkle with @sugar{to taste}(approx 2 tbsp).

Roll out the other half of the pastry. Moisten the top of the bottom layer of pastry and place the second piece on top. Press down on the pastry edges, making sure that they are properly sealed. Trim off any excess pastry with a knife in a downward motion, again using the plate as a guide. Flute the edges by pinching between fingers and thumb.

Prick the surface of the pastry lightly before placing the pie in the oven. Cook for 20 to ~{30%minutes}.

When the pie is cooked it should move slightly on the plate when shaken. Slide onto a serving plate, dust with caster sugar and serve.